From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:34:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/xenos: tile textures and cube maps

Only render-target-capable 2D textures were tiled. Cube maps and textures
in non-renderable formats (L8, A8, LA88, 16-bit float) stayed linear, and
Xenos lays out linear mips differently (rows aligned to 256 bytes, per
Xenia's texture_util) from fd2's layout: POT cubes and mipmapped
non-renderable textures sampled the wrong texels. The tiled layout already
matches the hardware, and the CPU (de)tiles on map, so tile 2D and cube
sampler textures too (not staging ones, not compressed formats).

dEQP-GLES2: 242 cases fixed, none regressed (98.3% -> 99.7%).

